silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_04_cheese_trap_and_identity_sections_02_controlled_category_use_yoneda_hom_leg_2 silm:hasExample "In 'P07CheeseTrapAndIdentityControlledCategoryUseYonedaHomLeg2', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, Felis catus / TSN 183798 is the ITIS taxonomy source row admitting the cat-classification arrow into D_Mittens; it is a source leg, not the cat." .
